    "result_text": "All 68 tests pass, build succeeds. The refactor is complete. Here's a summary of what I changed to unify `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `checkDigit` into a single `memberId`:\n\n## Format\n`memberId` = `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` (no separators), e.g. `NSW261A2B3C4D7`:\n- **REGION** \u2014 region from postcode (city fallback), via `Locality`\n- **FY** \u2014 2-digit fiscal year of the business-day-adjusted `registrationDate`\n- **HASH8** \u2014 first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName` (the region-and-hash identity's HASH8)\n- **CHK** \u2014 single Luhn check digit over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`\n\n## Changes\n- **New `MemberId.java`** util (replaces `CustomerCode.java`, deleted) \u2014 computes the unified id and exposes `regionOf(owner)` (now derived directly from `Locality`, since the id has no dash to parse).\n- **`AssignMemberId.java`** (renamed from `AssignCustomerCode`) \u2014 assigns `memberId`; collision de-duplication now applies to `memberId`.\n- **`Owner` entity** \u2014 `customerCode`/`customer_code` field \u2192 `memberId`/`member_id` with renamed getter/setter.\n- **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 removed `membershipNumber` and `checkDigit` mappings; added `memberId`; `locality` now uses `MemberId.regionOf`.\n- **`AuditOwnerCreated`** \u2014 audit line now carries `id`, `memberId`, `registrationDate`, `membershipLevel`; the structured event carries `memberId`.\n- **`OwnerCreatedEvent`** \u2014 record field & JSON key `customerCode` \u2192 `memberId`.\n- **`Timezone` / `OwnerSegment`** \u2014 reference `MemberId.regionOf`.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 removed `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, `membershipNumber` schema fields; added `memberId`.\n- **Schema SQL** (h2/hsqldb/mysql/postgres) \u2014 `customer_code` column \u2192 `member_id` (widened to 32 chars for the longer `UNKNOWN`-region + dedup case).\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 pipeline step `assignCustomerCode` \u2192 `assignMemberId`.\n\n`CheckDigit` and `FiscalYear` utilities are retained (now consumed by `MemberId`). The removed-field tests (Cp09/14/16/31), the new `memberId` tests (Cp32/56), collision (Cp41), fiscal year (Cp48), and audit tests (Cp21/43/53) all pass, along with the full suite (68/68).",
